enlighten|explain|VERB|Give understanding|To give someone information that helps them understand something.|giúp hiểu rõ; khai sáng|Could you enlighten me about the new procedure?|Bạn có thể giúp tôi hiểu rõ quy trình mới không?|Enlighten someone about something.|-
excite|interest|VERB|Make enthusiastic|To make someone feel eager or enthusiastic.|làm hào hứng; làm phấn khởi|The chance to travel excited the students.|Cơ hội đi du lịch khiến sinh viên hào hứng.|Transitive; excite a person.|-
engrave|carve|VERB|Cut a design into a surface|To cut words or a design into a hard surface.|khắc; chạm|They engraved her initials on the medal.|Họ khắc chữ viết tắt tên cô ấy lên huy chương.|Engrave something on something.|-
glucose|sugar|NOUN|Simple sugar|A simple sugar that living organisms use as an energy source.|đường glucose|The chart lists glucose among the sugars.|Biểu đồ liệt kê glucose trong các loại đường.|Uncountable substance; no health advice.|-
happily|cheerfully|ADVERB|With happiness|In a pleased or cheerful way.|vui vẻ|The children chatted happily on the bus.|Bọn trẻ vui vẻ trò chuyện trên xe buýt.|Manner adverb.|0
happily|willingly|ADVERB|Willingly|With readiness and no objection.|sẵn lòng|I would happily lend you my umbrella.|Tôi sẵn lòng cho bạn mượn ô.|Often would happily plus verb.|1
